// Design 185 unit 1, the same shift-range rule at the OTHER end of the
// pipeline. A `static_assert` is evaluated in codegen, where the target layout
// is authoritative, so it reaches the evaluator through its own frame — and a
// count outside `0..<width` has to read as "the condition is not a constant"
// there too, not as an assertion that quietly failed.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: static_assert condition is not a compile-time constant
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: shift count `64` out of range (0..<64)

static_assert((1 << 64) == 0, "a count at the width is not a count")

func main() {
    print("unreachable")
}
